{"id":"w446218","name":"Ata Ekuru (Ekuru Sauce)","author":"Wikibooks Cookbook contributors","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Ata_Ekuru_(Ekuru_Sauce)"},"via":{"name":"Wikibooks","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Ata_Ekuru_(Ekuru_Sauce)"},"image":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Pepper%20sauce.jpg?width=640","cuisine":"","country":"","region":"Global","course":"main","protein":"seafood","diet":0,"allergens":1851488,"minutes":70,"time":{"prep":25,"cook":45,"passive":0,"passiveWhy":[]},"timeEstimated":true,"servings":"","difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"item":"4 pieces tatase (red bell peppers)","qty":""},{"item":"6 pieces rodo (scotch bonnet chiles)","qty":""},{"item":"10 pieces shombo (fresh cayenne pepper)","qty":""},{"item":"1 alubosa (onion)","qty":""},{"item":"400 ml palm oil","qty":""},{"item":"Seasoning cubes","qty":""},{"item":"Salt","qty":""},{"item":"Fish (optional)","qty":""},{"item":"Ground crayfish (optional)","qty":""},{"item":"Beef (optional)","qty":""},{"item":"Ponmo (optional)","qty":""}],"steps":["Combine the bell pepper, chiles, and cayenne pepper. Blend to a chunky paste.","Heat the palm oil in a pan. After about 5 minutes, add the blended pepper mixture to the hot oil. Season with salt and bouillon cubes to taste, and add any of the optional ingredients as desired.","Let cook over medium-low heat for about 30–40 minutes, until well-cooked and the oil is floating on top of the sauce.","Serve with ekuru."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":null,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","lifestyle":125,"era":"modern"}